Example Package source media

Every package in this format ships a SOURCE.txt naming where its artwork, video and audio came
from. Nothing in the mod reads this file - it is for the people who install the package, and for
whoever has to answer for the content later. Both shipped packages carry one; a package posted
without one is asking its players to take the provenance on trust.

Say, for each asset: who made it, where you got it, on what date, and what you did to it.

Idle animation:
https://example.invalid/gallery/post/1234567

Scene clips, in manifest order:
https://example.invalid/gallery/post/1234568
https://example.invalid/gallery/post/1234569

The source GIF was converted to a transparent 10x8 PNG atlas (76 frames at 360x428). The clips
were resized to at most 640 pixels on the longest side, normalized to 24 fps and converted to
VP8/WebM, and retain stereo 48 kHz audio.

Capture sound: Example Sounds, "Whoosh" by someone.
Page: https://example.invalid/sounds/whoosh
Free under that site's content licence. The MP3 download was converted locally to mono 16-bit PCM
WAV for Unity playback on 2026-01-01. WAVE_FORMAT_EXTENSIBLE is refused even when it is 16-bit PCM
inside, so export plain PCM.

Funscripts: authored by hand against the handy2pro masters in this package, or state whose scripts
they started from.
